.env
__pycache__/
# data/ is committed on purpose. The CFBD key allows 1,000 calls a month;
# an empty data/ made every CI build refetch twelve of them, including two
# finished seasons that can never change again. Pull once, save, commit.
data/*.tmp
site/index.html
!history/
site/history.html

# Forecasts are perishable and fetched at build time — see weather.py.
data/weather_cache.json

# build.py's archive-skip stamp: a digest of every input that can change what
# a finished season renders to, written after 2024 and 2025 are rebuilt so the
# next build can skip them. Local build state, like the cache above. A stamp
# committed from one checkout is a claim about another machine's output
# directory, and the failure it buys is silent: a season kept because its
# inputs "have not changed" when that checkout never rendered it. Nine seconds
# is not worth an archive quietly serving last month's design.
site/*/.inputs
